**HomeShield Architecture — Decoupled Zero-Hop Edge Architecture**

The router handles network-wide DNS interception with zero hops, while Smart TV debloating runs as an independent companion utility over LAN ADB.

---

### Data Flow Summary

| Stage | Component | Key Operation |
|-------|-----------|---------------|
| **Tier 0** | GitHub Actions | Pull 29 feeds → Deduplicate 285k+ domains → Apply whitelist → Publish to CDN |
| **Daily Sync** | Router Daemon | HTTP pull every 86400s → FNV-1a delta check → Atomic memory swap |
| **Enforcement** | iptables/ip6tables | IPv4 REDIRECT 53→dnsmasq \| IPv6 REJECT 53/853 (Anti-DoT) |
| **Resolution** | dnsmasq | Blocked→`0.0.0.0`/`::` \| Whitelisted→Forward to WAN |
| **Clients** | All LAN devices | Zero-config protection (Mobile, PC, Smart TV, IoT) |
| **Companion** | CleanYourTV CLI | ADB discovery → Debloat 1,100+ packages → Auto-rollback script |

---

### Mermaid Rendering

To view this diagram:
- **GitHub/GitLab**: Renders natively in `.md` files
- **VS Code**: Install "Markdown Preview Mermaid Support" extension
- **Obsidian**: Enable Mermaid in Settings → Editor
- **Online**: Paste into [mermaid.live](https://mermaid.live/)